From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:51:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 119/159] [ae-patch] Show the effort a Claude session runs at
 when none was picked

With no pick the runner passes no --effort and Claude Code takes effortLevel
from its settings, which the web never saw, so the Effort menu showed no
level and no check. At each launch without --effort the runner reads the
level in Claude's precedence (managed, workspace local, workspace, then the
launch account's user settings) and writes it to the session label
ae.claude_effort_default, never to reasoning_effort, so nothing is pinned
and a pick made mid-launch is not overwritten. The menu shows that level as
"High (default)" with High checked, or "Claude default" when no file names
one.
